  CustomStringTableItem "{6B3D000000000106}" {
   Id "OVT-Faction_US_Occupying"
   Target_en_us "US forces hold the island. They garrison its bases and radio towers and patrol its towns, and their uniform is the one that works as a disguise."
   Target_de_de "US-Streitkräfte halten die Insel besetzt. Sie bemannen deren Stützpunkte und Funktürme und patrouillieren in den Ortschaften – und ihre Uniform ist es, die als Tarnung dient."
   Target_ru_ru "Американские силы удерживают остров. Они размещают гарнизоны на базах и радиовышках и патрулируют города. Их форма подходит для маскировки."
   Target_uk_ua "Острів перебуває під контролем сил США. Вони утримують гарнізони на базах і радіовежах та патрулюють населені пункти, а їхню уніформу можна використовувати для маскування."
   Comment "Campaign-setup screen (UI/Layouts/Menu/StartGameMenu.layout, the OccupyingFactionDescription widget), shown under the Occupying Faction spinner when US is selected. Resolved by faction KEY, not by spinner index, in OVT_StartGameContext.ResolveOccupyingFactionDescription. LENGTH BUDGET: this widget is right-aligned, wrapped, font 18 in an 880px column and must not exceed TWO lines (about 210 characters) or the description block starts eating the gap above the Start button. TONE: informs, never instructs; no imperative and no implied order of play. FACT-CHECKED 2026-08-09. 'US forces hold the island': the occupying faction is what OVT_StartGameContext.OnSpinOccupyingFaction sets through OVT_OverthrowConfigComponent.SetOccupyingFaction:275, and US is one of the two spinner options (OVT_OverthrowFactionManager.et:24-31 registers USSR, US, FIA and CIV; OVT_StartGameContext.c:98 drops FIA because FIA_OverthrowData.conf:3 is m_bIsPlayable 1, and :99 drops CIV). Garrisons and patrols: OVT_InfantrySpawningDeploymentModule.c:486 (patrol/garrison groups sized by patrolGroupsMin/Max), Configs/Deployment/Deployment_TownPatrol.conf:26 (m_iAllowedFactionTypes OCCUPYING_FACTION - only the occupier patrols towns) and Configs/Deployment/Deployment_TowerGarrison.conf (m_iAllowedFactionTypes OCCUPYING_FACTION, m_iAllowedLocationTypes RADIO_TOWER - radio towers are garrisoned by the same deployment system as of 2026-08-17). Disguise: OVT_PlayerWantedComponent.c:111 IsDisguisedAsOccupying, with 7 live consumers including SCR_CharacterDamageManagerComponent.c:27,69,121. This string and OVT-Faction_USSR_Occupying differ ONLY in the faction name, and that is correct rather than lazy: US_OverthrowData.conf and USSR_OverthrowData.conf differ only in which prefabs the generic slot names resolve to, so no mechanical per-faction claim survives a fact-check (cut C6). CORRECTED 2026-08-18 by virtualization/base-defense-migration Phase 8: OVT_BaseUpgradeDefensePosition is DELETED and defenseGroupsBaseMax now has ZERO readers tree-wide (still authored in every Configs/Difficulty/Difficulty_*.conf and still declared at OVT_DifficultySettings.c:45, but read by nothing). The player-facing claim survives on patrolGroupsMin/Max alone, which still scales monotonically across the five presets; base-defence group sizes are now set per deployment module and the amount of defence a faction can afford scales through baseResourcesPerTick/resourcesPerTick into the deployment pool. The old :416 read site is now OVT_InfantrySpawningDeploymentModule.c:486."
   DevNote ""
   Repro ""
   ActorGender NONE
   Terminology NONE
   Status DEVELOPMENT_PENDING
   NonTranslatable 0
   MaxLength 0
