  CustomStringTableItem "{6B3B000000000166}" {
   Id "OVT-FieldManual_BaseCapture_Text5"
   Target_en_us "Nothing taken is held for good. The occupying faction settles on one place it means to take back and works toward it over hours of visible activity, so a counter attack arrives at the end of a build-up rather than out of nowhere; the Counter Attacks page follows that build-up from the first truck to the assault. Towns and cities are chosen the same way and fought over the same way. A radio tower is a quieter business: it is taken by clearing the garrison standing at it, and a tower near whatever the occupiers are working toward can be walked back the other way by a team that reaches it and holds it long enough. Bases, towns and towers can all change hands more than once in a campaign."
   Target_de_de "Nichts, was eingenommen wurde, bleibt dauerhaft in der eigenen Hand. Die Besatzungsmacht hält Reserven zurück und investiert sie in ihre verbliebenen Stützpunkte; verfügt sie über einen Überschuss, wählt sie einen von der Widerstandsbewegung eroberten Stützpunkt aus, um ihn zurückzuerobern, und wartet anschließend eine Weile, bevor sie es erneut versucht. Um Städte und Funktürme wird auf ganz ähnliche Weise gekämpft, sodass ein Ort im Verlauf einer Kampagne mehrfach den Besitzer wechseln kann."
   Target_ru_ru "Ничто из захваченного не остаётся за вами навсегда. Оккупирующая фракция выбирает одно место, которое намерена вернуть, и работает над этим в течение нескольких часов видимой активности, так что контратака прибывает в конце подготовки, а не из ниоткуда; страница «Контратаки» описывает эту подготовку от первого грузовика до штурма. Города и крупные населённые пункты выбираются таким же образом и захватываются так же. Радиовышки — более тихое дело: их захватывают, зачищая гарнизон, а вышку, расположенную рядом с тем, на что нацелились оккупанты, можно отбить обратно, если команда доберётся до неё и удержит достаточно долго. Базы, города и вышки могут менять владельца несколько раз за кампанию."
   Target_uk_ua "Жоден захоплений об'єкт не забігається за вами назавжди. Ворог накопичує резерви й розподіляє їх між утримуваними базами. Коли ресурсів стає достатньо, окупанти обирають одну з втрачених баз і починають контратаку, а після штурму беруть паузу перед наступним нападом. Захоплення міст і радіовеж відбувається за аналогічною механікою, тож контроль над локаціями може переходити з рук у руки неодноразово протягом кампанії."
   Comment "Field Manual - Capturing Bases page, body paragraph under the 'The Answer Back' header. Five sentences, no rich-text markup. FACT-CHECKED 2026-08-08 against OVT_OccupyingFactionManager (reserve resources spent per base via OVT_BaseControllerComponent.SpendResources:281-315; the counter-attack branch at :1178-1194 fires on a surplus, picks a base the resistance holds, calls StartBaseQRF and then sets m_bCounterAttackTimeout from the difficulty setting counterAttackTimeout), StartTownQRF:826-878 and OnQRFFinishedTown:917-960 (towns), and OVT_BaseUpgradeSpecops.OnUpdate:38-65 (radio towers are retaken by a specops team, ChangeRadioTowerControl at :65). The surplus threshold, the random roll and the timeout are deliberately not quoted. CORRECTED 2026-08-17 by virtualization/integration Phase 8: the sentence used to read 'Towns and radio towers are fought over in much the same way', which is no longer true of towers - a tower is not a QRF battle and has no ticking control counter, it flips the moment its garrison is wiped (OVT_RadioTowerCaptureBehaviorDeploymentModule.c:89 and :122-124). Towers now have their own Field Manual page, 'Patrols and Garrisons'. CORRECTED AGAIN 2026-08-18 by virtualization/base-defense-migration Phase 8: the tower sentence used to end 'and it is taken back by a specialist team sent out from an occupied base', which cited OVT_BaseUpgradeSpecops.OnUpdate - that class and its 600 s recapture timer are DELETED (decision D3, specops dropped with no replacement). The ONLY writer of ChangeRadioTowerControl left in the tree is OVT_RadioTowerCaptureBehaviorDeploymentModule.c:124, which always passes config.GetPlayerFactionIndex(), so no code path returns a tower to the occupying faction; the replacement clause states exactly that. The 'a place can change hands more than once' sentence was narrowed to bases and towns for the same reason. The earlier citation of SpendResources:281-315 in this comment is also dead - base defence is now bought from the deployment pool (see OccupyingForces_Text); the counter-attack half of this paragraph is unaffected and re-verified at OVT_OccupyingFactionManager.c:1420-1429 (m_iResources > 2000, a random roll, StartBaseQRF on a base the resistance holds, then m_bCounterAttackTimeout from the difficulty setting counterAttackTimeout). REWRITTEN 2026-08-19 by occupying/counter-attacks Phase 10, because TWO of its five sentences had become false. (1) 'when it has more than it needs it will pick a base the resistance took and come back for it, then wait a while before trying again' described the surplus roll and the timeout, BOTH DELETED in this feature's Phase 1 - the immediately preceding CORRECTED-AGAIN note's own re-verification at :1420-1429 is now dead code and is left above only as a record. Counter-attacks are now a single objective run through three phases by OVT_ObjectiveDirectorComponent.c, with the battle itself gated on OVT_ObjectivePhaseRules.TownPhase3Gate / BasePhase3Gate plus the daylight predicate; nothing anywhere rolls dice for a target. (2) 'once it is lost the occupying faction has no way of taking it back' was true only between base-defense-migration deleting OVT_BaseUpgradeSpecops and this feature landing: OVT_TowerRecaptureBehaviorDeploymentModule.c:100-106 now calls ChangeRadioTowerControl with the DEPLOYMENT's faction after a team holds the tower (m_fHoldRadius 80, hold time objectiveTowerRecaptureHoldSeconds, 600 on Normal), authored on Configs/Deployment/Deployment_ObjectiveTowerRecapture.conf and sent only during the harassment phase of a nearby objective (OVT_ObjectiveConditionDeploymentModule m_iRequiredPhase 1). Hence the last sentence widens back out to include towers. 'Towns and cities are chosen the same way' is the selection set in OVT_ObjectiveSelection - resistance-held bases, towns and cities, never villages, towers or FOBs. ⚠ Target_de_de and Target_uk_ua still carry the pre-rewrite text and need re-translating. RE-FACT-CHECKED 2026-08-21 by occupying/objectives Phase 8. The body is unchanged and still true; THREE citations in the note above are now dead. (1) The battle is no longer gated on OVT_ObjectivePhaseRules.TownPhase3Gate / BasePhase3Gate: those statics survive but nothing in production calls them, and the gate is now the authored condition modules on each plan's ForwardBase phase (town: OVT_SupportBelowObjectiveCondition m_iSupportThreshold 25; base: OVT_ProgressAtLeastObjectiveCondition m_iRequired -1 = objectiveSabotageMissionsRequired), plus OVT_AssetUpObjectiveCondition, OVT_ReserveAtLeastObjectiveCondition and OVT_DaylightWindowObjectiveCondition. (2) The three phases are no longer an enum: they are authored names, \"Harassment\", \"ForwardBase\" and \"CounterAttack\", in Configs/Objective/Objective_TownOffensive.conf and Objective_BaseOffensive.conf, and a mod may rename them. (3) The tower-recapture deployment is NOT sent only during harassment: OVT_ObjectiveConditionDeploymentModule now spans phases by NAME and Deployment_ObjectiveTowerRecapture.conf:53-54 authors m_sFromPhase \"Harassment\" through m_sThroughPhase \"ForwardBase\". m_fHoldRadius 80 and objectiveTowerRecaptureHoldSeconds 600 on Normal are unchanged."
