  CustomStringTableItem "{6B3C000000000112}" {
   Id "OVT-Tutorial_BasesFirstCapture_Body"
   Target_en_us "You have just entered the restricted zone of a base. You will become wanted if you are seen here. In order to capture bases you must reach the flag at the center and trigger a battle. The battle will be decided by how many players (and recruits) hold the middle of the base against how many occupying soldiers are still there. Control runs both ways: the occupying faction settles on one place it means to take back and builds up against it over time, and a base the resistance holds can be that place."
   Target_de_de "Du hast gerade das Sperrgebiet einer Basis betreten. Wenn du hier gesehen wirst, wirst du gesucht. Um Basen einzunehmen, musst du die Flagge in der Mitte erreichen und eine Schlacht auslösen. Der Ausgang der Schlacht hängt davon ab, wie viele Spieler (und Rekruten) die Mitte der Basis halten und wie viele Soldaten der Besatzungsmacht noch dort sind. Die Kontrolle kann in beide Richtungen wechseln: Die Besatzungsmacht hält Reserven vor und setzt überschüssige Kräfte ein, um eine vom Widerstand gehaltene Basis zurückzuerobern."
   Target_ru_ru "Вы только что вошли в запретную зону базы. Если вас здесь заметят, вы станете розыскиваемым. Чтобы захватить базу, нужно добраться до флага в центре и начать битву. Битва будет решаться тем, сколько игроков (и рекрутов) удерживают центр базы против оставшихся солдат оккупантов. Контроль работает в обе стороны: оккупационная фракция выбирает одно место, которое намерена вернуть, и готовится к этому со временем, и база, удерживаемая сопротивлением, может стать таким местом."
   Target_uk_ua "Ви щойно увійшли до забороненої зони бази. Якщо вас тут помітять, вас оголосять у розшук. Щоб захопити базу, потрібно дістатися прапора в центрі та розпочати бій. Результат бою залежатиме від того, скільки гравців (і новобранців) утримують центр бази, порівняно з кількістю окупаційних солдатів, що ще залишилися на ній. Контроль працює в обидва боки: окупаційна фракція має резерви й витрачає їх надлишок на спроби відбити базу, яку утримує опір."
   Comment "Body of the 'bases-first-capture' tutorial tip (single page, HUD popup, wraps inside a 460px panel - two short sentences at most). No rich-text markup. DELIVERY CONSTRAINT, read before rewording: this entry is triggered by BASE_CONTROL_CHANGE, which is a 300 m proximity fan-out with NO acting player and which fires in BOTH directions (OVT_TutorialManagerComponent.c:34, 345-355). The text must therefore never say 'you captured', never assume the reader did anything, and must read correctly for a bystander and for a player who has just lost a base. Sandbox tone rule: describes the system, never instructs. FACT-CHECKED 2026-08-09 for tutorial-content Phase 2. Sentence 1: OVT_QRFControllerComponent.CheckUpdatePoints:100-192 - once the reinforcement timer expires the component counts occupying-faction AI and player-controlled entities within QRF_POINT_RANGE = 220 every ten seconds, moves m_iPoints towards whichever side has more, and control changes when the score reaches the difficulty setting QRFPointsToWin in either direction, at which point m_OnFinished fires and OVT_OccupyingFactionManager.ChangeBaseControl:895-915 flips the faction. DO NOT describe capture as taking or planting a flag: the flag material follows the faction change (OVT_BaseControllerComponent.SetControllingFaction:143-152, UpdateFlagMaterial:99-116) and never causes it. Sentence 2: ChangeBaseControl:895-915 notifies the whole server in both directions and moves threat by 250 each way, and OVT_OccupyingFactionManager:1217-1226 spends a reserve surplus on a QRF against a base the resistance holds (RE-CITED 2026-08-17, Phase 8 of virtualization/integration; the branch was at :1178-1194). ALSO CORRECTED 2026-08-17: the DELIVERY CONSTRAINT above describes BASE_CONTROL_CHANGE, but Configs/Tutorials/basesFirstCapture.conf now binds this entry to PLAYER_ENTER_BASE (OVT_TutorialTrigger.c:44), which is a per-player crossing into a base's restricted radius and carries no payload - the 'never say you captured' rule still holds, for the different reason that the reader has captured nothing yet. NOTE FOR FUTURE EDITS, REWRITTEN 2026-08-18 by virtualization/base-defense-migration Phase 8 (the old note said base garrisons were NOT migrated and that the kill switch still guarded their legacy spawners - both statements are now false; the kill switch file is deleted and base defence IS on the virtualization layer as nine deployment configs). Every sentence of this body was RE-VERIFIED on 2026-08-18 and none of them changed: the restricted-zone/wanted clause, the flag (OVT_CaptureBaseAction is authored on Prefabs/Structures/Military/Flags/BaseFlag_US.et:18 and BaseFlag_USSR.et:28 as well as on Prefabs/Controllers/OVT_BaseController.et:74), the QRF point count and the counter-attack clause (OVT_OccupyingFactionManager.c:1420-1429, which still spends m_iResources and is an epic-level exclusion). Base defence persistence claims still belong on #OVT-FieldManual_OccupyingForces_Text2 and _Text7, not here: this popup is 460 px wide and already over its own two-sentence budget. Compresses #OVT-FieldManual_BaseCapture_Text, _Text3 and _Text5. Point totals and ranges are not quoted: the win total is a difficulty setting and the ranges are internal constants. CORRECTED 2026-08-19 by occupying/counter-attacks Phase 10 - the LAST SENTENCE WAS FALSE AS SHIPPED. It read 'the occupying faction keeps reserves and spends a surplus of them on retaking a base the resistance holds', which is the retired hourly surplus roll at the OVT_OccupyingFactionManager.c:1420-1429 this comment kept re-citing; that branch, m_bCounterAttackTimeout and the counterAttackTimeout difficulty field were all DELETED in this feature's Phase 1, and grep -rn 'counterAttackTimeout' Scripts/ Configs/ Prefabs/ is empty. The replacement states the shipped machine: OVT_ObjectiveDirectorComponent.c holds ONE objective at a time, selected without any random roll by OVT_ObjectiveSelection from the resistance-held bases, towns and cities, and works toward it through harassment, a forward base and finally the counter attack. Deliberately no numbers and no phase names in a 460 px popup - the page it points at, #OVT-FieldManual_BaseCapture_Title, now names the Counter Attacks page for the detail. Tone re-checked: 'can be that place' informs and implies no action. ⚠ Target_de_de and Target_uk_ua still carry the retired-mechanic sentence and need re-translating. RE-FACT-CHECKED 2026-08-21 by occupying/objectives Phase 8. THE BODY NEEDED NO EDIT and every clause was re-checked: one objective at a time is still the shipped cap (both plans author m_iMaxInstances 1 and the director floors m_iMaxConcurrentObjectives at 1), and 'builds up against it over time' still describes the ramp. Two things behind it moved. (1) The target is no longer picked by the director reading OVT_ObjectiveSelection: each plan in Configs/Objective/overthrowObjectives.conf carries its own selector with authored weights, and there is still no random roll (m_fChance 100 short-circuits the draw). (2) The three phases are authored DATA now, named \"Harassment\", \"ForwardBase\" and \"CounterAttack\" in the plan .confs, which a mod may rename. That makes the existing rule - this 460 px popup names no phase and no number - a hard requirement rather than a space-saving choice: a phase name written here could not be kept true for a modded registry. The Field Manual deep link (#OVT-FieldManual_BaseCapture_Title, which points on to Counter Attacks) is where the detail stays."
